{
  "note": [
    "The row layout every shell must agree on, as data rather than as code.",
    "",
    "`grid::painted_rows` is the specification; `web/src/protocol.ts` hand-mirrors it in TypeScript",
    "and `render.ts` paints from that mirror rather than from the wasm core. Both walks are tested,",
    "but until this file they were tested against fixtures hand-written in their own language, so",
    "nothing would have caught them drifting apart. This is the table both are pinned to.",
    "",
    "`root` is wire-format `aether_protocol::ui::Element`; `measured` is wire-format",
    "`grid::Measured`. `rows` is the flattened output: one entry per painted row, in order, with",
    "only the fields both languages can produce. Rows need not be consecutive \u2014 an element with",
    "nothing loaded leaves a gap, which is the point of case `a-gap-where-nothing-is-loaded`.",
    "",
    "Vertical only, deliberately. `PaintedRow` carries no horizontal coordinate today; when stage",
    "3.4 gives it one, `x` and `width` are added here and the painters' own column tests (which are",
    "per-shell, because a cell is not a pixel) keep covering what a cell is worth.",
    "",
    "Rows carry `left`/`right` \u2014 the cells the boxes around them claim, not a width: the walk is a",
    "pure function of the tree and never learns the viewport's size, so each shell subtracts these",
    "from the width it has. `edge` rows are a box's own border/padding rows, which are not tree",
    "nodes; their `join` is derived from sibling order, never sent."
  ],
